    "Added missing Agno and LangGraph optional dependency entrypoints to both distributions",
    "Added isolated feature performance/differential matrix with explicit upstream automatic, FP32 and FP16 autocast modes",
    "Corrected legacy benchmark FP32 label by disabling upstream row-gated autocast explicitly",
    "Validated unchanged standalone SDK live HTTP assertions against MLX and Core ML native models, extended/tournament and strict modes",
    "Avoided repeated Core ML sequence-shape changes inside logical batches while retaining token masks and row order",
    "Added native adaptive Core ML bundle assembly, identity checks, lazy graph selection and resource cleanup; existing single-graph bundles retain their behavior",
    "Exported B=1/2/4/16 graph sets for all three checkpoints, preserving full context capacities and source weights",
    "Validated all fifteen adaptive feature workload outputs against upstream; repeated the batch comparison in fresh processes",
    "Validated complete public outputs and 100 mixed repeated calls on each adaptive checkpoint",
    "Added native warmup API to both backends and honored MLX compile_warmup with upstream best-effort automatic/explicit-error behavior",
    "Rebuilt both distributions and exercised final inference-only wheels offline, including warmup and adaptive large/tail batches",
    "Audited 341 public surface entries against pinned upstream; native backend introspection explicitly implemented",
    "Completed exact official calibration temperature/binning differential and save/load roundtrip on real native logits for all three models per backend; repeated pseudo-label records are compatibility evidence only",
    "Fixed MLX local_files_only support and removed unsupported Core ML Router keyword",
    "Corrected pure FP32 public reference by disabling upstream automatic MPS autocast; retained historical mixed public reference for traceability",
    "Passed full public-output and 63-question numerical checks plus 100 repeated calls for all three native models in both precisions against pure FP32; decimal comparator preserves original numeric tolerance"
